{"id":"936f3a2e7f0558815feee8fb5e566a2d008bceb921dff173077f1b68b25b60e1","pubkey":"32310997f6b37b6cd60bb15a28e9a14badddfbf0875a7de24c69123a0c1e64cc","created_at":1782870086,"content":"blogを書きました。とても楽しい作品でした。東映やりたい放題すぎる\n\n『免許返納！？』観てきました♪ https://showhyuga.blogspot.com/2026/07/blog-post.html","tags":[]}
{"id":"8f27fdf9ae4306efd92b93e3870cec4f6894005f622f85d6d24023853c3b5678","pubkey":"ef89ee45550f7377284d31e49fc57e5732ffc2b95a7bf35d0f1291d6fa278758","created_at":1782869432,"content":"https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#blend-state\n\nこれを読めば良さそうだ。\n\ndstが先に描かれていた色でsrcがこれから描く色。\nたとえば0 * dst + 1 * srcだと「新しい色で上書き」する。\nalpha * dst + (1 - alpha) * srcだと「透明度を考慮して適切に背景を透過して描画する」といった感じ。\n\nこのdstやsrcに対する係数や、それらの項をつなぐ演算(上の例では+)を列挙型で指定できる。","tags":[["e","701a4d63f51fba6e4b8323313997857a8db616462dd7fc9d13853ecb71ba8f8c","","root"],["p","ef89ee45550f7377284d31e49fc57e5732ffc2b95a7bf35d0f1291d6fa278758"],["r","https://gpuweb.github.io/gpuweb/#blend-state"]]}
{"id":"a5fc3b229e5582cb1fccff2862c3c17b6ff30377fbefc97cf055ba6f1cc7d04e","pubkey":"b7274d28e3e983bf720db4b4a12a31f5c7ef262320d05c25ec90489ac99628cb","created_at":1782869201,"content":"Yeah, it's the experimenting with various clients that can sometimes result in things getting nuked.\n\nThe absolute best tool I have ever found for fixing things when that happens is Luminostr: https://tsukemonogit.github.io/luminostr/\n\nVery simple interface. Just plug in your npub and the kind number of note that got nuked, and then tell it how many relays you want it so search for that note on. I typically just leave it at the max number of relays (400). The search takes longer, but then you can be pretty confident that the previous version of the note you are looking for will be found. You can then choose to publish the previous version of that note to restore what was nuked.\n\nThe only thing that makes this tool a bit less user friendly is that it expects you will know the kind number you are looking for, rather than providing you with a dropdown to select \"short text note\" or \"follow list\" and such. So here's a breakdown of the main note kinds you may find this tool useful for:\n\nKind 3 - Your follow list. These things get nuked all the time when switching between clients.\n\nKind 10002 - Your Outbox/Inbox relay list. That's the one I just looked up on Luminostr for you to find out when it got wiped.\n\nKind 10000 - Your mute list. Like the follow list, I hear about this one getting nuked a lot.\n\nKind 10012 - Your favorite relays list. Not to be confused with your regular relay list for outbox/inbox. This list is just relays you like to browse. I recently had mine get wiped and had to restore it using Luminostr.\n\nIf you want a list of other note kinds and what they are for, you can find one at https://github.com/nostr-protocol/nips","tags":[["e","4ee7cbd8faab145b546128ab8503072d9210894d18f366874d271270aded2987","wss://nostr.bitcoinist.org","root","bc02e0a6c0f01ad9cb57a2b0f8ef8241bc5ff979ce4452ce9e243de457756725"],["e","f8db9d5f7ae57b1d8b406192077a59f20ebc7925ccd49f266769113fe8da6ef8","wss://relay.primal.net/","reply","bc02e0a6c0f01ad9cb57a2b0f8ef8241bc5ff979ce4452ce9e243de457756725"],["p","c230edd34ca5c8318bf4592ac056cde37519d395c0904c37ea1c650b8ad4a712"],["p","bc02e0a6c0f01ad9cb57a2b0f8ef8241bc5ff979ce4452ce9e243de457756725"]]}
